page({file:'methodology.html',title:`Methodology | ${NAME}`,desc:'How VPSLedger reads, verifies and normalizes VPS prices.',body:`<section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Methodology</div><h1>How the ledger is kept.</h1></section><ol class="lede"><li>Prices come only from the provider’s own pricing page or official public API (Vultr, Linode, Azure Retail Prices). Each row stores the source URL and check date.</li><li>A row is <b>verified</b> when price and specs were read on that date; otherwise <b>unverified</b>, with unknowns left blank. We never estimate a price.</li><li>True monthly cost = list (or renewal) price + IPv4 + backups (optional) + max(0, egress − included transfer) × overage rate. Unpublished fees count as $0 and are flagged.</li><li>EUR prices convert at ${FX_EUR_USD} USD/EUR, the ECB reference rate for ${FX.date} (<a href="${FX.source}">source</a>). Prices exclude VAT/sales tax.</li><li>Hourly-billed clouds use 730 hours/month.</li><li id="savings"><b>Savings figures.</b> Computed at build time from verified rows only, at ${EG} TB/month egress with backups on. “Equivalent” plans have 1–2× the target vCPU and RAM. Yearly gap = (priciest − cheapest true monthly cost) × 12. Hidden fees = true cost − list price at 1 TB. Renewal jump = renewal − intro price. Unverified fees (e.g. an overage rate we could not read on the provider’s page) count as $0 in these claims, so gaps are conservative. Plans whose egress price is not in the ledger are excluded when egress exceeds their allowance. Raw figures: <a href="/api/stats.json">/api/stats.json</a>.</li><li>A weekly script diffs every source page; confirmed changes enter the price log.</li></ol>`});
page({file:'data.html',title:`${NAME} data — JSON & CSV`,desc:'Free JSON and CSV of VPS plan prices with sources. CC BY 4.0.',ld:[ORG_LD,{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Dataset',name:`${NAME} VPS price ledger`,url:SITE+'/data.html',license:'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/',dateModified:lastChecked,distribution:[{'@type':'DataDownload',encodingFormat:'application/json',contentUrl:SITE+'/api/plans.json'},{'@type':'DataDownload',encodingFormat:'text/csv',contentUrl:SITE+'/api/plans.csv'}]}],body:`<section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Data · CC BY 4.0</div><h1>Machine-readable ledger.</h1><p class="lede"><b>Answer:</b> Download verified VPS plan prices as JSON or CSV. Every row has a source URL and check date. Please attribute “${NAME}” with a link to ${SITE}/.</p></section><dl class="kv"><dt>Plans + providers (JSON)</dt><dd><a href="/api/plans.json">/api/plans.json</a></dd><dt>Plans (CSV)</dt><dd><a href="/api/plans.csv">/api/plans.csv</a></dd><dt>Price log (JSON)</dt><dd><a href="/api/changes.json">/api/changes.json</a></dd><dt>Price log (CSV)</dt><dd><a href="/api/changes.csv">/api/changes.csv</a></dd><dt>Stats</dt><dd><a href="/api/stats.json">/api/stats.json</a></dd><dt>LLM summary</dt><dd><a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> · <a href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a></dd></dl><div class="panel"><h3 class="h3">Cite this</h3><pre style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px">${esc(`VPSLedger VPS price ledger (${SITE}/api/plans.json, ${SITE}/api/plans.csv). License: CC BY 4.0. Please attribute "VPSLedger" with a link to ${SITE}/.`)}</pre></div><p class="note">Public CSV/JSON are free under CC BY 4.0. Pro adds watched-plan alerts and richer export history.</p>`});
